03:24:16,850 --> 03:24:18,510
 So, edit mode, everything is selected.

3695
03:24:18,510 --> 03:24:25,750
 If I drop my weight to zero and then say assign, then go back into weight paint mode, everything is black.

3696
03:24:25,750 --> 03:24:29,810
 Because this vertex group thing here, this is the weight paint, right?

3697
03:24:29,890 --> 03:24:32,950
 So, you can select everything if you want and just make it entirely one.

3698
03:24:32,950 --> 03:24:35,810
 Or you can make it entirely zero.

3699
03:24:35,810 --> 03:24:39,830
 Anyways, now that I've got that, as you can tell, I've got front faces on.

3700
03:24:39,830 --> 03:24:41,510
 Now I can do my painting, all right?

3701
03:24:41,510 --> 03:24:43,030
 So, where do you want your sprinkles to go?

3702
03:24:43,030 --> 03:24:44,970
 You just do that painting, right?

3703
03:24:44,970 --> 03:24:52,200
 And you can have, you know, you can change the weight of the brush as well if you want there to be, like, a lot that's

3704
03:24:52,200 --> 03:24:53,970
 kind of just, like, on the edge, right?

3705
03:24:53,970 --> 03:24:55,110
 You could do something like that.

3706
03:24:55,330 --> 03:25:00,690
 But generally, you know, it doesn't have to be that, you know, that perfect.

3707
03:25:00,690 --> 03:25:04,330
 You know, I'm just doing this as an example of how you could, you know, really do it.

3708
03:25:04,330 --> 03:25:06,730
 You could also go, like, weight one and then turn the strength down.

3709
03:25:06,730 --> 03:25:11,530
 And then now as you paint, you get, like, you know, different amounts of buildup.

3710
03:25:11,530 --> 03:25:13,350
 But, you know, how detailed do you want?

3711
03:25:14,850 --> 03:25:19,990
 Like, do you want, I don't think anybody's ever going to look at your donut render and go, like, wow, the distribution

3712
03:25:19,990 --> 03:25:21,610
 of those sprinkles is amazing.

3713
03:25:21,610 --> 03:25:24,510
 You did a great job distributing the sprinkles.

