03:27:53,190 --> 03:28:00,960
 Now, the big question people have when they're looking at this, they go, how do you stop the sprinkles from intersecting

3757
03:28:00,960 --> 03:28:02,050
 each other?

3758
03:28:02,050 --> 03:28:08,170
 And, unfortunately, there's not an easy answer, because this is not easy to do.

3759
03:28:08,170 --> 03:28:11,710
 There's such a thing as, like, circle packing.

3760
03:28:11,710 --> 03:28:19,230
 That's the closest thing, which is, like, you could run an algorithm to try to combine circles of different radiuses

3761
03:28:19,230 --> 03:28:21,650
 to kind of fit together as best they could.

3762
03:28:21,650 --> 03:28:23,430
 But just, it's complex.

3763
03:28:23,430 --> 03:28:27,210
 That's kind of like a simulation, and we just, we can't do it easily here.

3764
03:28:27,210 --> 03:28:34,890
 The closest thing we have is called Distribution Method Poisson Disc, which, when you click that,

3765
03:28:34,890 --> 03:28:39,090
 and by the way, you can only see that option if you're using Density Method, not Amount.

3766
03:28:39,090 --> 03:28:48,070
 So Amount will let you actually use a specific amount of sprinkles, but then you don't get this extra option here.

3767
03:28:48,230 --> 03:28:52,530
 Whereas Density bases it on the scale of the object in relation to the scene and yada yada.

3768
03:28:52,530 --> 03:28:57,170
 But anyways, Poisson Disc gives you this little setting, minimum distance.

3769
03:28:57,170 --> 03:29:02,730
 And what it does is, essentially, every single one of these points here, it goes, there's a point, there's a point,

3770
03:29:02,730 --> 03:29:03,610
 there's a point, there's a point.

3771
03:29:03,650 --> 03:29:10,290
 And then when you increase this value by whatever amount, it will add a circle around it, right?

3772
03:29:10,290 --> 03:29:17,980
 And if you increase that circle, and you increase that circle, right, eventually, if this one, for example, had a value

3773
03:29:17,980 --> 03:29:22,050
 of this size, this little dot here would be removed.

3774
03:29:22,110 --> 03:29:25,450
 Because it is now colliding with the value of this one.

3775
03:29:25,450 --> 03:29:27,130
 So this one would override that one.

3776
03:29:27,130 --> 03:29:28,750
 So this one gets X'd.

3777
03:29:28,750 --> 03:29:32,850
 So if we increase this, you can see that is exactly what happens.

3778
03:29:32,850 --> 03:29:34,190
 All right.

3779
03:29:34,190 --> 03:29:36,730
 So I'm holding down Shift as I just play with that value there.

3780
03:29:36,730 --> 03:29:39,730
 But you can see that's removed some of the intersections.

3781
03:29:40,410 --> 03:29:41,930
 But there are still some more.

3782
03:29:41,930 --> 03:29:44,550
 So you might be tempted, like, all right, let's increase that even more.

