03:56:49,830 --> 03:56:52,950
 So this, you can see, this is a soft color.

4264
03:56:52,950 --> 03:56:56,410
 This is like moonlighting, but it just needs to be a little bit,

4265
03:56:56,410 --> 03:57:00,870
 just so that there's the hint that there is skylighting along with the sun.

4266
03:57:00,870 --> 03:57:07,170
 Now, the other big factor that it's missing is that skylighting is not casting shadows like this, right?

4267
03:57:07,410 --> 03:57:12,210
 If the sun was away and it was just being lit by the sun, like think of like an overcast day, right?

4268
03:57:12,210 --> 03:57:16,050
 The sky itself, the entire dome is the size of the light.

4269
03:57:16,050 --> 03:57:21,010
 So the radius of our lamp here needs to increase, right?

4270
03:57:21,010 --> 03:57:21,690
 By a lot.

4271
03:57:22,750 --> 03:57:27,450
 Now, this is a very underused value.

4272
03:57:27,450 --> 03:57:32,010
 Like it's one of the most important values when it comes to lighting is the radius of something

4273
03:57:32,010 --> 03:57:34,530
 because it's the softness of the shadow.

4274
03:57:34,530 --> 03:57:36,330
 As an example, let's just bring this in.

4275
03:57:36,330 --> 03:57:36,850
 Actually, hang on.

4276
03:57:36,850 --> 03:57:39,790
 Let's just increase this so we can actually see it.

4277
03:57:39,790 --> 03:57:40,470
 What can I do?

4278
03:57:40,470 --> 03:57:40,970
 Exposure.

4279
03:57:40,970 --> 03:57:41,430
 There we go.

4280
03:57:41,430 --> 03:57:42,250
 All right.

4281
03:57:42,250 --> 03:57:44,010
 So this is like the default.

4282
03:57:44,010 --> 03:57:45,490
 It comes in like this, okay?

4283
03:57:45,490 --> 03:57:48,150
 And you can see how harsh those shadows are.

4284
03:57:48,150 --> 03:57:52,550
 So as a rule, harsh shadow is very good at revealing detail.

4285
03:57:52,750 --> 03:57:57,270
 So we often use a lot at Polygon because we need to show the detail of textures along a surface.

4286
03:57:57,270 --> 03:58:02,050
 So if you want to highlight the sprinkles or something like that, you would use a very small

4287
03:58:02,050 --> 03:58:02,870
 radius like this.

4288
03:58:02,870 --> 03:58:05,190
 So it's really sharp shadows.

4289
03:58:05,190 --> 03:58:10,490
 Whereas if you want to reveal more of the form and just the overall color of a surface,

4290
03:58:10,490 --> 03:58:13,930
 that is when you would use a larger radius, right?

4291
03:58:13,930 --> 03:58:14,810
 As a general rule.

4292
03:58:14,810 --> 03:58:17,930
 And it has a huge impact on lighting.

4293
03:58:17,930 --> 03:58:19,990
 The other big thing is distance.

4294
03:58:20,550 --> 03:58:22,790
 So there's, I mentioned briefly, the inverse square law.

4295
03:58:22,790 --> 03:58:26,170
 A lot of beginners, you know, they go like, oh, it's like skylighting.

